<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Paragorio</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Paragorio is a Romanesque church in Noli, on the Ligurian coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, built in the 11th century on the site of an early Christian church. It served as the cathedral of the diocese of Noli, created in 1239, until the see moved to another church in the town. Restored in the late 19th century, it is one of the best-preserved Romanesque churches in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liguria">Liguria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-paragorio.jpg" alt="San Paragorio" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davide Papalini · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Noli-IMG_1592.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
